{"wikiid":630275,"langid":"en","namespace":"CATEGORY","title":"Fairphone 6","revisionid":1426942,"contents_raw":"== Repairability ==\n\n[link|https:\/\/support.fairphone.com\/hc\/en-us\/articles\/24590029621138-The-Fairphone-Gen-6-Replace-a-Spare-Part|Fairphone 6 repair guides]\n\n== Background ==\n\nThe Fairphone 6 (or now technically \"The Fairphone Gen. 6\") is, as the name suggests, the sixth generation repairable smartphone from Dutch company Fairphone. It keeps\u2014and builds on\u2014the same part modularity and easy repairability as previous generations, e.g., easily-replaceable batteries, screens, ports, and cameras. Fairphone has been continually committed to [link|https:\/\/support.fairphone.com\/hc\/en-us\/articles\/115001041206-Find-fix-an-issue-yourself|supporting DIY repair], and this continues into the 6th generation.\n\nThe Fairphone 6 features a 6.31-inch LTPO OLED display, a Snapdragon 7s Gen 3, a 50 MP Sony camera, and customizable back cover accessories.\n\nThe Fairphone 6 is available in Black, Green, or White colorways.\n\n== Identification ==\n\nYou can identify the Fairphone 6 by its triple camera array, \"fairphone\" text near the bottom, and two exposed Torx screws near the middle seam. \"***Model FP6***\" is printed on the side rail.\n\n== Technical Specifications ==\n\n***Display***\n\n* 6.31-inch 1116 x 2484 (20:9, 431 ppi) LTPO P-OLED\n* 10\u2013120 Hz variable refresh rate\n* 1400 nits peak brightness\n* Corning Gorilla Glass 7i\n\n***Processor***\n\n* Qualcomm Snapdragon 7s Gen 3 (64-bit Kryo CPU)\n* Adreno GPU\n\n***RAM***\n\n* 8 GB LPDDR5\n\n***Storage***\n\n* 256 GB internal (UFS 3.1)\n* microSD support (up to 2 TB)\n\n***Battery***\n\n* Removable 4415 mAh Li-ion\n\n***Cameras***\n\n* 50 MP Sony Lytia 700C main camera (with OIS)\n* 13MP ''\u0192''2.2 ultra wide camera\n\n***Connectivity***\n\n* Wi-Fi 6E\n* Bluetooth 5.4 LE\n* NFC\n* 5G nano-SIM + eSIM\n\n***Durability***\n\n* IP55\n* MIL-810H\n\n***Sensors***\n\n* Fingerprint reader\n* Facial recognition\n* Hall sensor\n* Accelerometer\n* Barometer\n* Gyroscope\n* Compass\n* Light sensor\n* Proximity sensor\n\n***Dimensions and Weight***\n\n* 156.5 x 73.3 x 9.6 mm (6.17 x 2.89 x 0.38 in)\n* 193 g (0.43 lbs)\n\n== Additional Information ==\n\n* [link|https:\/\/en.wikipedia.org\/wiki\/Fairphone|Wikipedia: Fairphone]\n* [link|https:\/\/shop.fairphone.com\/the-fairphone-gen-6|Fairphone Official: The Fairphone 6]\n* [link|https:\/\/support.fairphone.com\/hc\/en-us|Fairphone Official: Support]\n* [link|https:\/\/support.fairphone.com\/hc\/en-us\/articles\/115001041206-Find-fix-an-issue-yourself|Fairphone Official: Find & fix an issue yourself]\n* [link|https:\/\/www.theverge.com\/news\/692248\/fairphone-6-smartphone-repairable-modular-accessories-murena|The Verge: Fairphone 6 Review]","contents_json":{"type":"doc","content":[{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Repairability"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/support.fairphone.com\/hc\/en-us\/articles\/24590029621138-The-Fairphone-Gen-6-Replace-a-Spare-Part","target":false}}],"text":"Fairphone 6 repair guides"}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Background"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fairphone 6 (or now technically \"The Fairphone Gen. 6\") is, as the name suggests, the sixth generation repairable smartphone from Dutch company Fairphone. It keeps\u2014and builds on\u2014the same part modularity and easy repairability as previous generations, e.g., easily-replaceable batteries, screens, ports, and cameras. Fairphone has been continually committed to "},{"type":"text","marks":[{"type":"link","attrs":{"href":"https:\/\/support.fairphone.com\/hc\/en-us\/articles\/115001041206-Find-fix-an-issue-yourself","target":false}}],"text":"supporting DIY repair"},{"type":"text","text":", and this continues into the 6th generation."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fairphone 6 features a 6.31-inch LTPO OLED display, a Snapdragon 7s Gen 3, a 50 MP Sony camera, and customizable back cover accessories."}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Fairphone 6 is available in Black, Green, or White colorways."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Identification"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You can identify the Fairphone 6 by its triple camera array, \"fairphone\" text near the bottom, and two exposed Torx screws near the middle seam. \""},{"type":"text","text":"Model FP6","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]},{"type":"text","text":"\" is printed on the side rail."}]},{"type":"heading","attrs":{"level":2},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Technical Specifications"}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Display","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","attrs":[],"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"6.31-inch 1116 x 2484 (20:9, 431 ppi) LTPO P-OLED"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"10\u2013120 Hz variable refresh rate"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"1400 nits peak brightness"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Corning Gorilla Glass 7i"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Processor","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","attrs":[],"content":[{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Qualcomm Snapdragon 7s Gen 3 (64-bit Kryo CPU)"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","content":[{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Adreno GPU"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","content":[{"type":"text","text":"RAM","marks":[{"type":"bold"}]}]},{"type":"bulletList","attrs":[],"content":[{"type":"listItem","co